 "method_limits": [
  "the population is E433's published rows (constdirs_latest.json) carrying a fragment; rows are deduplicated to (fragment, resolved_directory) targets, so row counts and target counts are different units and are published side by side",
  "a site is attributed only when its composing chain ends in the fragment literal: a site that builds the name from a variable, an f-string, or a loop is outside this scan and is not counted as absent",
  "the base is resolved one hop through module-level constants (string literal, __file__/dirname shape, another name); a base bound inside a function stays base_unresolved rather than being guessed from its spelling",
  "existence is tested on the current work tree, so a gitignored runtime cache that this machine never wrote reads as absent exactly like a mis-composed in-tree path"
 ]
